# Coding conventions

## Files & naming
- Library components: `src/components/<PascalCase>.tsx`, one component family per file. Registry/CLI/docs slugs are kebab-case (`AlertDialog` → `alert-dialog`), derived automatically.
- Hooks: `src/hooks/useXxx.ts`; animation hooks live in `src/animations/` and are re-exported from `animations/index.ts`.
- Tests: `src/components/__tests__/<Name>.test.tsx`; stories: `src/stories/<Name>.stories.tsx`.
- Docs app imports use the `@/` alias (`@/components/...`, `@/lib/...`). Library uses relative imports only (the CLI transformer rewrites `../x` and `./PascalCase` imports — keep that shape).

## Component pattern (library)
- First line `"use client";` (all 56 components have it).
- `export interface XProps extends Omit<HTMLAttributes<...>, "color">, SketchProps` with JSDoc on every prop (`@default`, `@example`) — JSDoc is extracted into registry/MCP docs.
- `forwardRef` with a named inner function, then `X.displayName = "X"`. Compose refs with `assignRef(ref, node)`.
- Compound APIs: export the parts AND attach them via `Object.assign(Root, { Header, ... })` (Card, Table, Accordion, Field).
- Context-only parts throw when used outside the root: `throw new Error("Table parts must be used inside <Table>.")`.

```tsx
export const Button = memo(
  forwardRef<HTMLButtonElement, ButtonProps>(function Button(
    { variant = "primary", size: sizeProp = "md", roughness, seed, sketchColor, animate, ...rest },
    ref,
  ) {
    const theme = useSketchTheme(sketchColor);
    const shouldAnimate = useAnimate(animate);
    const resolvedSeed = useResolvedSeed(seed);
    // ...
  }),
);
Button.displayName = "Button";
```

- Derive per-part seeds with `deriveSeed(resolvedSeed, "hover")` so parts redraw together on Shuffle.
- Icon-only controls call `warnIfMissingAriaLabel(...)` from `primitives/icon`.
- Sizes go through `resolveSize` + `CONTROL_SIZE_STYLES` from `primitives/size` (`DoodleSize`).

## TypeScript
- `strict`, `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`, `noUnusedLocals`, `noUnusedParameters` (packages/tsconfig/base.json). Use `!` only after an explicit length/index check.
- `import type` / inline `type` specifiers for type-only imports.
- Style: double quotes, semicolons, trailing commas, 2-space indent (no Prettier config exists — match surrounding code).

## Exports
- Every public component, its props type, and variant types are re-exported from `src/index.ts`. Unexported = not public.
